 ## Background
-Preprocessed Marching Cubes is an implementation variant of the Marching Cubes algorithm that incorporates preprocessing steps to improve the quality of the extracted mesh. It is commonly used in medical imaging and 3D reconstruction pipelines where raw voxel data may contain noise or artifacts. The method is implemented in the `niimath` tool and described in unofficial documentation [S1, unofficial].
+Preprocessed Marching Cubes extracts a triangle mesh from a 3D scalar volume using Marching Cubes, with optional preprocessing (smoothing, connected-component filtering, edge darkening) to isolate the largest object, fill internal bubbles, and improve surface boundary detection [S1, unofficial]. The method is implemented in the `niimath` tool and described in unofficial documentation [S1, unofficial].
 
